2. Disclosure keyboard operability — confirmed live:
   - `#major-expenses-definitions-toggle` is a real `<button
     aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="major-expenses-definitions-panel">`
     (not a div/onclick).
   - Tab reaches it directly (`.focus()` succeeds); Enter opens the panel
     (`panel.open` true, `aria-expanded` → "true"); Space on the open
     panel closes it again (`aria-expanded` → "false") — both keys wired,
     state stays synced.
   - Per-row expand chevrons (`button.major-expense-row-toggle`,
     `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls`) are likewise real buttons, keyboard
     Enter toggles `tbody[data-open]` and the row's `aria-expanded`.

3. Delete-only-when-expanded, verified against the actual a11y tree (not
   just CSS), using Playwright's real actionability checks (`isVisible()`,
   `focus()`, `click()` timeouts) rather than raw `offsetParent` (Chromium's
   newer `<details>` `::details-content` implementation makes descendant
   `offsetParent`/`getComputedStyle` unreliable as a hidden-content proxy —
   confirmed this discrepancy directly, then re-verified with Playwright's
   real visibility/interactability semantics):
   - Fresh load (definitions panel collapsed): delete button `isVisible()`
     = false, not focusable.
   - Definitions panel opened, individual row still collapsed (default):
     delete `isVisible()` = false; 60 Tab presses from the definitions
     toggle never land on it (confirmed by walking `document.activeElement`
     each press) — matches "collapsed detail row exposes no delete
     control to keyboard/AT."
   - Row expanded via its own toggle: delete `isVisible()` = true,
     `.focus()` succeeds, `aria-label="Delete major expense <name>"`
     present and descriptive. CSS confirmed:
     `#major-expenses-list tbody[data-open="false"] > tr.major-expense-detail-row
     { display: none; }` (pre-existing rule, unchanged) is what removes it
     from the tab order/AT tree while collapsed.

4. Heading structure — rendered DOM (all `<details>` open): exactly one
